WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:59.292
Yeah, I always get very mixed results
with those plant identification apps.

00:05:59.325 --> 00:06:02.161
It's saying a Chickasaw plum,

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:05.898
but earlier it was saying it was a cherry plum

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:08.501
I've only seen one of them here.

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:10.503
And there are other, like, European plums.

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:12.839
Two of them close to the Land Rover

00:06:12.839 --> 00:06:15.441
and one in front of the house.

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:17.243
And none of them give fruit.

00:06:17.243 --> 00:06:18.945
Only on the one there I've seen

00:06:18.945 --> 00:06:21.948
one little plum some years ago.

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:29.422
That could be a few reasons, actually.

00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:32.592
There's not enough trees for cross
pollination

00:06:32.592 --> 00:06:35.595
or the trees
are not compatible with each other.

00:06:36.396 --> 00:06:38.097
Or too far out?

00:06:38.097 --> 00:06:39.432
Too far away from each other.

00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:42.435
And that could be the case.

00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:43.669
They need to be pruned.

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:45.571
Some of them.

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:48.174
So this one I could prune.

00:06:48.174 --> 00:06:50.977
I mean, it's doing beautifully,
but it grew very tall.

00:06:52.445 --> 00:06:54.947
Because
it was all the old birches around it.

00:06:54.947 --> 00:06:56.449
So they're all fighting for the light.

00:06:56.449 --> 00:07:00.186
So they'll do better now,
but they need to be pruned.

00:07:01.754 --> 00:07:05.057
But I think also a big reason
for no pollination

00:07:05.057 --> 00:07:08.060
is that the bees are not here yet.

00:07:08.895 --> 00:07:11.898
We're at 1200 meters, so it's quite cold.

00:07:12.832 --> 00:07:15.001
These trees are blossoming

00:07:15.001 --> 00:07:17.970
now in April,
but the bees kind of arrive in May.

00:07:18.271 --> 00:07:21.607
When it warms up a bit more,
because I saw a few last week

00:07:21.607 --> 00:07:24.610
when it was quite warm and sunny.

00:07:24.744 --> 00:07:28.414
And the bumblebee is already here,
but just a few.

00:07:29.182 --> 00:07:30.183
And this is a cold day.

00:07:30.183 --> 00:07:32.418
It's like seven degrees Celsius.

00:07:32.418 --> 00:07:34.320
So they,

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.656
they don't get out.

00:07:36.656 --> 00:07:39.659
So that could also be
the reason that bees are too late.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:41.227
But, you know,

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:43.863
we'll see. The apple trees...

00:07:43.863 --> 00:07:47.033
those have been doing well,
but they're also very small yet.

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:50.937
So I think I'm going to pinch some flowers
because it was very heavy with apples

00:07:51.204 --> 00:07:53.172
last year, which is great.

00:07:53.172 --> 00:07:56.175
But the tree needs some time to grow.

00:07:58.077 --> 00:07:59.946
So yeah, there is another pear tree.

00:07:59.946 --> 00:08:02.949
I should make an overview of all
the fruit trees that are actually here.

00:08:03.816 --> 00:08:08.888
And do some pruning before winter

00:08:08.888 --> 00:08:13.826
and plant a few more, let them grow, and
see in a few years

00:08:14.327 --> 00:08:17.330
how they are doing.

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:47.613
Work.

00:11:42.868 --> 00:11:45.871
This is going to be the last stone.

00:11:46.172 --> 00:11:48.908
That is going to go in the building,

00:11:48.908 --> 00:11:50.109
the very last one.

00:11:50.109 --> 00:11:51.711
Then it is finished,

00:11:51.711 --> 00:11:54.714
almost a year of building.

00:11:56.882 --> 00:12:01.854
The first stone, this one,

00:12:02.488 --> 00:12:05.357
was laid in, I think, mid-May last year.

00:12:06.459 --> 00:12:09.595
The foundation was done in November 2024.

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:12.998
And we had a long winter break.

00:12:12.998 --> 00:12:19.171
So we did the floor, I think, late
April last year and then started the walls in May,

00:12:19.171 --> 00:12:22.141
all summer laying stone until

00:12:23.542 --> 00:12:26.545
about October I started building the scaffolding,

00:12:26.912 --> 00:12:29.882
mid-October.

00:12:29.882 --> 00:12:33.586
The beams went in in November, I think.

00:12:34.386 --> 00:12:37.389
And then the roof was built
in the winter. So...

00:12:39.191 --> 00:12:42.194
It's been a good run.

00:12:42.495 --> 00:12:46.265
It might be interesting to do some calculations of how

00:12:46.499 --> 00:12:49.034
how heavy this little building actually is,

00:12:49.034 --> 00:12:52.037
because I think it's quite a lot.

00:14:05.711 --> 00:14:08.247
Okay.

00:14:08.247 --> 00:14:16.555
I’ve calculated the weight of the foundation,
the floor, walls, and the roof using AI.

00:14:16.555 --> 00:14:20.726
So I've put in all the dimensions
I mentioned,

00:14:20.726 --> 00:14:23.762
dimensions of the window,
dimensions of the lintels.

00:14:25.631 --> 00:14:28.634
Also photos of how the wall is built.

00:14:28.801 --> 00:14:32.104
It's still a rough estimation, but

00:14:32.671 --> 00:14:35.674
to kind of see how much mortar is used
and how much stone.

00:14:37.743 --> 00:14:41.313
So concrete foundation:

00:14:41.647 --> 00:14:44.650
it's almost 17,000 kg.

00:14:45.351 --> 00:14:48.220
I put the numbers here in pounds.

00:14:48.220 --> 00:14:50.422
Floor slab:

00:14:50.422 --> 00:14:53.125
a little over 10,000 kg,

00:14:53.125 --> 00:14:57.129
the walls about 30... 31,000 kg.

00:14:58.264 --> 00:14:59.865
Roof:

00:14:59.865 --> 00:15:02.635
this is just the stones,
not the wood.

00:15:02.635 --> 00:15:05.638
6.7, close to 7,000.

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:09.408
And then the wood.

00:15:09.408 --> 00:15:13.178
I didn't calculate this,
but I guess that's about 3,000 kilos.

00:15:13.345 --> 00:15:15.447
The total:

00:15:15.447 --> 00:15:20.119
64,430 kg

00:15:20.119 --> 00:15:24.823
and 142,000 pounds.

00:15:24.823 --> 00:15:26.325
And then to think that every stone

00:15:26.325 --> 00:15:29.428
is picked up twice or three times,

00:15:29.762 --> 00:15:32.765
once to collect it, sort things out,

00:15:32.831 --> 00:15:35.834
and then to pick it up, put it in the wall.

00:15:36.702 --> 00:15:39.705
It's a lot! But it has been fun.

00:15:39.972 --> 00:15:42.975
It might be interesting
to also do the calculation of the costs,

00:15:43.142 --> 00:15:46.679
how much it costs, but I'll do that
after I've done electricity

00:15:46.946 --> 00:15:49.848
and everything.

00:15:49.848 --> 00:15:52.851
It costs less than it weighs,

00:15:53.052 --> 00:15:55.487
for sure.

00:34:20.291 --> 00:34:23.261
One of.

00:37:45.096 --> 00:37:50.801
The underbody shield was bent after being stuck in the snow many times.

00:40:28.859 --> 00:40:31.862
Do you want to go outside?

00:40:55.686 --> 00:40:58.689
It’s their first time outside.

00:40:58.989 --> 00:41:01.992
A bit hesitant, still.

00:41:02.259 --> 00:41:05.863
But it’s greening up,
so it's nice for them to eat,

00:41:06.330 --> 00:41:09.333
eat grass and all kinds of things.

00:41:11.135 --> 00:41:11.368
Yeah.

00:41:11.368 --> 00:41:13.003
Yeah, I'm making good progress with the walls.

00:41:13.003 --> 00:41:15.873
That pointing machine is just,

00:41:15.873 --> 00:41:18.876
it goes so fast.

00:41:19.977 --> 00:41:22.913
Not only fast,
it also goes really deep inside the wall.

00:41:22.913 --> 00:41:25.916
So it really fills up the joints.

00:41:27.218 --> 00:41:29.787
Next week we'll finish that up
because I have some help.

00:41:29.787 --> 00:41:31.222
It’s better to do it with two people.

00:41:31.222 --> 00:41:35.526
So one mixing and also stirring the bucket,
because you want to have like a

00:41:36.961 --> 00:41:40.364
not too liquid mix, firm enough.

00:41:41.732 --> 00:41:46.337
But then for the pump to be able to handle
it, it needs to be stirred all the time.

00:41:46.737 --> 00:41:51.375
So a second person is needed to do it well.

00:41:51.375 --> 00:41:53.577
And maybe we'll also do the floor.

00:41:53.577 --> 00:41:55.980
I'm going to do

00:41:55.980 --> 00:41:58.716
self-leveling screed,

00:41:58.716 --> 00:42:01.719
a cement product,
not just normal cement, but

00:42:01.952 --> 00:42:04.321
like a liquid cement

00:42:04.321 --> 00:42:06.123
which is made for it.

00:42:06.123 --> 00:42:08.425
And it'll make a nice floor.

00:42:08.425 --> 00:42:11.428
And after that, I can put stuff inside.

00:42:13.898 --> 00:42:18.135
But before I get machines in, I think I should work on the soil.

00:42:18.402 --> 00:42:19.270
So there’s...

00:42:19.270 --> 00:42:22.339
I see the concrete is slightly
damp in the corners.

00:42:22.840 --> 00:42:26.710
It's not too bad, but you can
see that the foundation is getting wet.

00:42:28.212 --> 00:42:30.948
At the back,
I need to dig out the hill a bit more.

00:42:32.716 --> 00:42:36.153
So do some soil
work and put in some drainage as well

00:42:36.921 --> 00:42:38.322
so it stays...

00:42:38.322 --> 00:42:41.325
The humidity needs to be quite low

00:42:41.559 --> 00:42:42.293
in the summer.

00:42:42.293 --> 00:42:45.296
That's more difficult here.

00:42:45.863 --> 00:42:48.432
And also, I need...
yeah, there’s quite a bit of digging work to do.

00:42:48.432 --> 00:42:49.967
I need to update the solar panels.

00:42:49.967 --> 00:42:53.070
I need to dig in a new line
towards the workshop

00:42:53.070 --> 00:42:56.073
because I need two groups there.

00:42:58.042 --> 00:43:01.045
Hey, guys.

00:43:03.681 --> 00:43:05.082
Those are bilberries.

00:43:05.082 --> 00:43:08.085
They’re not ripe yet.

00:43:12.690 --> 00:43:13.123
Yeah, I'm

00:43:13.123 --> 00:43:16.493
going to replace the solar panels and

00:43:18.062 --> 00:43:21.065
run two new [electrical] groups towards the workshop.

00:43:21.365 --> 00:43:22.766
In the beginning, I didn't think so big.

00:43:22.766 --> 00:43:25.536
I didn't know I was going to be with Ela.

00:43:25.536 --> 00:43:28.472
I didn't know I was going to build
a workshop for woodworking with machines.

00:43:28.472 --> 00:43:30.674
So I'm expanding a bit.

00:43:34.278 --> 00:43:34.712
But yeah.

00:43:34.712 --> 00:43:36.614
Beautiful days...

00:43:36.614 --> 00:43:40.784
I'm taking my time with the garden beds
because it's heavy work for my back.

00:43:40.784 --> 00:43:43.754
The rotation with the shoveling.

00:43:43.754 --> 00:43:46.290
I have to take that slow
because I feel it.

00:43:46.290 --> 00:43:49.827
All the other work is okay,
but that is the worst work,

00:43:50.761 --> 00:43:53.731
so it takes time.

00:43:56.433 --> 00:43:59.403
Come back!

